  "published": "2026-11-11T23:28:36.717Z",
  "releaseNotes": "9.7.5\nFixed: the data of a font from a collection (.ttc or .otc) was the collection from the font header to the end of the file, with offsets from the start of the collection, so it was not a valid font program. A PDF viewer could not load the embedded font and drew another one. The font is now rebuilt on its own.\nNew: targets net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 as well as net6.0 and netstandard2.0.\nNew: ResourceStreamLoader reads a font from an assembly resource (rsrc://Namespace.File.ext, AssemblyName).\n\n9.7.4\nFixed a data race in TTFStringMeasurer's per-character glyph metric cache: a shared measurer written from multiple threads at once (concurrent document rendering) could corrupt the underlying Dictionary, surfacing as InvalidOperationException/ArgumentException/NullReferenceException out of MeasureChars. Cache is now a ConcurrentDictionary, written through the indexer.\nVersioning aligned with the Scryber.Core engine version from this release onward - the PackageVersion had drifted from what was actually last published (9.2.0) since 6.0.3.3-beta; the source itself was current, only the project file's version metadata had lagged.\n\n9.2.0\nNow supports the otf, ttf, and ttc file formats for font reading and measuring.\nCompatible with net standard 2.0 and net 6.0.\n\nThere is a change in usage to the Scryber.OpenType.TypefaceReader along with returning a LineSize struct, rather than a System.Drawing.SizeF struct.\n\nAdded support for measurement honoring the non-breaking space (char 160) and breaking preferentially on a hypen if it is flagged in the type measurement options.\n\nThis is the base type for reading OpenType, TTF and TTC font files used in scryber.core, but is independent from any PDF creation requirements.\n\nSee the read me at https://github.com/richard-scryber/Scryber.Core.OpenType for more usage information.",
